**Existing generation checks**: only `const g = routeLoad.generation;` at line 1226, guarding the two `isCurrent(g)` returns at 1230/1233 — and that pair protects only the nested inactive-panel reload, exactly as `handleDeactivateConfirm`'s mirror-image `g` (line 1105) protects only its own inactive-panel reload, not the outer flag.

**The trap, confirmed present**: `g` at line 1226 is captured AFTER the first await (`reinstateMember`, line 1215) and after a SECOND await (`loadForSelected()`, line 1218) that itself unconditionally bumps `routeLoad.generation` on every call. So `g` is exactly the same kind of already-rebased capture #287 found and rejected in the pre-fix `handleDeactivateConfirm` — reusing it for the outer `finally` (line 1244) would produce a guard that is always true relative to itself and silently does nothing. **A NEW entry-level capture is required** (the `handleDeactivateConfirm` precedent calls this `gEntry`, captured at line 1028, before `deactivatePending = true` and before any await) — no usable capture currently exists for this handler's outer flag.

**Outer `finally` (lines 1243-1245)**: unconditionally clears `reinstatePending = null;` with NO generation guard at all — not `if (g === routeLoad.generation) reinstatePending = null;`, just a bare write. This is the finally-not-guarded half of the bug the issue names.

**Does `reset` clear it?** No. `reset`'s full body is `src/routes/roster/+page.svelte:155-237`; it explicitly clears `removePending` (173), `pendingDeactivateId`/`deactivateRefusal`/`deactivateActionError`/`deactivatePending` (176-183), `inviteActionPending` (194), and the record-editor trio (205-207), plus (isSwitch-gated, 221-236) `showInactive`/`inactiveRows`/`inactiveLoadError`/the three invite maps. `reinstatePending` does not appear anywhere in that block — confirmed absent by reading the whole callback. So a collective switch mid-reinstate leaves the NEW collective's Reinstate button (line 5009, `disabled={reinstatePending !== null}`) permanently disabled, holding the OLD collective's memberId, exactly as #296 describes.
